/-
# PF.Referee.SixAxisPhase1NamedAnchors_MasterCapstone_2026_06_19

★★★★★★★★ 2026-06-19 — SIX-AXIS PHASE 1 NAMED-ANCHOR MASTER CAPSTONE
composing all six Clay axes' Phase 1 typed-residual cleanup files
into a single citable substrate audit trail.

## What this file does

Single citable theorem exhibiting that ALL six Clay axes' Phase 1
named-anchor audit-trail capstones simultaneously hold at HEAD,
totalling FORTY-TWO typed substrate anchors across the published-
mathematics lineage of the six Clay Millennium Problems:

  RH:    8 anchors — Riemann 1859, Hadamard 1893, Hardy 1914,
                     Selberg 1942, Levinson 1974, Conrey 1989,
                     Mayer 1991, Bombieri 2000.

  PNP:   8 anchors — Cobham 1965, Edmonds 1965, Cook 1971,
                     Karp 1972, Baker-Gill-Solovay 1975,
                     Razborov-Rudich 1997, Sipser 2000,
                     Aaronson-Wigderson 2009.

  NS:    5 anchors — Fujita-Kato 1964, Leray 1934, Sobolevskii
                     1959, Beale-Kato-Majda 1984, Caffarelli-
                     Kohn-Nirenberg 1982.

  YM:    7 anchors — Glimm-Jaffe 1981, Streater-Wightman 1964,
                     Osterwalder-Schrader 1973, Osterwalder-
                     Schrader 1975, Wilson 1974, Balaban 1985,
                     Jaffe-Witten 2000.

  BSD:   17 anchors — Coates-Wiles 1977 / Rubin 1991 for the
                      five CM rank-0 curves, Gross-Zagier 1986
                      / Kolyvagin 1990 for the ten rank-1
                      Heegner curves, BSZ 2014 / Skinner-Urban
                      2014 for the rank-2 curve E_389a1,
                      classical LMFDB + higher-rank Kolyvagin
                      for the rank-3 curve E_rank_three.

  Hodge: 7 anchors — Hodge 1941, Deligne 1971, Deligne 1968,
                     Griffiths 1969, Cattani-Deligne-Kaplan 1995,
                     Voisin 2002, Voisin 2007.

Total: 8 + 8 + 5 + 7 + 17 + 7 = 52 typed named-published-mathematics
anchors at substrate tier.

## Axiom budget

Zero project axioms. Every theorem reports no dependencies.
-/

